1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,600
Five apples plus five
apples is ten apples.

2
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:06,751
Five rupees plus five
rupees is ten rupees.

3
00:00:07,151 --> 00:00:10,720
Adding is easy, as long as
the things are the same kind.

4
00:00:11,170 --> 00:00:13,892
Aarav rides five metres in five seconds.

5
00:00:13,892 --> 00:00:16,615
He writes five metres plus five seconds.

6
00:00:16,965 --> 00:00:18,557
His calculator says ten.

7
00:00:18,557 --> 00:00:19,457
Ten what?

8
00:00:19,329 --> 00:00:20,629
Something is wrong.

9
00:00:21,129 --> 00:00:23,832
By the end, you will see exactly why.

10
00:00:23,832 --> 00:00:25,587
The answer is dimensions.

11
00:00:26,237 --> 00:00:27,793
So what are dimensions?

12
00:00:28,143 --> 00:00:31,956
Every physical quantity is built
from the seven base quantities.

13
00:00:32,356 --> 00:00:34,762
In mechanics, three of them are enough.

14
00:00:34,762 --> 00:00:36,256
Mass, length and time.

15
00:00:36,656 --> 00:00:38,901
We write them with square brackets.

16
00:00:38,901 --> 00:00:42,914
Capital M for mass, capital L
for length, capital T for time.

17
00:00:43,314 --> 00:00:47,221
The dimensions of a quantity are the
powers of the base quantities needed

18
00:00:47,221 --> 00:00:48,121
to build it.

19
00:00:48,769 --> 00:00:52,178
Let's watch Aarav's bicycle
on our motion notebook.

20
00:00:52,528 --> 00:00:55,038
It covers five metres in each second.

21
00:00:55,038 --> 00:00:56,572
Distance is a length.

22
00:00:56,572 --> 00:00:58,007
Its dimension is L.

23
00:00:58,407 --> 00:00:59,434
Time is T.

24
00:00:59,434 --> 00:01:01,984
Speed is distance divided by time.

25
00:01:01,984 --> 00:01:05,771
So speed is L over T,
or LT to the minus one.

26
00:01:06,171 --> 00:01:07,470
Now he speeds up.

27
00:01:07,470 --> 00:01:09,517
Let's replay it in slow motion.

28
00:01:09,517 --> 00:01:13,106
Every second, the speed grows
by two metres per second.

29
00:01:13,556 --> 00:01:17,287
Acceleration is a change
in speed, divided by time.

30
00:01:17,287 --> 00:01:21,223
So it is LT to the minus
one, divided by T again.

31
00:01:21,723 --> 00:01:23,942
That gives LT to the minus two.

32
00:01:23,942 --> 00:01:25,313
Look at the graphs.

33
00:01:25,313 --> 00:01:28,922
One slope gives speed, the
other slope gives acceleration.

34
00:01:29,572 --> 00:01:32,605
Let's build the dimensions
of area, step by step.

35
00:01:32,955 --> 00:01:33,855
Step one.

36
00:01:33,846 --> 00:01:36,236
Area equals length times breadth.

37
00:01:36,986 --> 00:01:37,886
Step two.

38
00:01:37,841 --> 00:01:38,916
Length is L.

39
00:01:38,916 --> 00:01:42,046
Breadth is also a length, so it is L too.

40
00:01:42,796 --> 00:01:43,815
Step three.

41
00:01:43,815 --> 00:01:45,765
L times L is L squared.

42
00:01:45,765 --> 00:01:48,502
So area has the dimension L squared.

43
00:01:49,252 --> 00:01:50,152
Step four.

44
00:01:50,148 --> 00:01:51,632
No mass, no time.

45
00:01:51,632 --> 00:01:55,579
So we write M to the zero,
L squared, T to the zero.

46
00:01:56,329 --> 00:01:59,214
The zero powers say: no mass, no time.

47
00:01:59,214 --> 00:02:00,723
Only length, twice.

48
00:02:01,373 --> 00:02:04,925
Now the reasoning for volume
and density, link by link.

49
00:02:05,275 --> 00:02:08,281
Volume is length times
breadth times height.

50
00:02:08,281 --> 00:02:09,402
Three lengths.

51
00:02:09,402 --> 00:02:10,429
So L cubed.

52
00:02:10,829 --> 00:02:13,761
Density is mass divided by volume.

53
00:02:13,761 --> 00:02:14,942
Mass is M.

54
00:02:14,942 --> 00:02:16,706
Volume is L cubed.

55
00:02:17,106 --> 00:02:19,328
So density is M over L cubed.

56
00:02:19,328 --> 00:02:21,717
That is ML to the minus three.

57
00:02:21,717 --> 00:02:24,138
A negative power means we divided.

58
00:02:24,738 --> 00:02:25,844
Remember this.

59
00:02:25,844 --> 00:02:28,832
Dimensions are the powers of M, L and T.

60
00:02:28,832 --> 00:02:33,132
You can only add or subtract
quantities with the same dimensions.

61
00:02:33,882 --> 00:02:35,021
Side by side.

62
00:02:35,021 --> 00:02:37,721
On the left, distance, five metres.

63
00:02:37,721 --> 00:02:39,240
Its dimension is L.

64
00:02:39,640 --> 00:02:42,032
On the right, time, five seconds.

65
00:02:42,032 --> 00:02:43,432
Its dimension is T.

66
00:02:43,432 --> 00:02:46,251
L is not T, so they can never be added.

67
00:02:46,851 --> 00:02:47,876
Now you try.

68
00:02:47,876 --> 00:02:52,815
Can you add a speed of five metres per
second to a speed of eighteen kilometres

69
00:02:52,815 --> 00:02:53,715
per hour?

70
00:02:53,631 --> 00:02:54,906
Pause and decide.

71
00:02:58,106 --> 00:02:59,006
Yes!

72
00:02:58,640 --> 00:03:00,977
Both are LT to the minus one.

73
00:03:00,977 --> 00:03:05,840
Eighteen kilometres per hour is five
metres per second, so the sum is ten

74
00:03:05,840 --> 00:03:07,234
metres per second.

75
00:03:07,884 --> 00:03:09,268
Here is a surprise.

76
00:03:09,268 --> 00:03:12,362
Different quantities can
share the same dimensions.

77
00:03:12,712 --> 00:03:14,998
Speed is LT to the minus one.

78
00:03:14,998 --> 00:03:17,478
An angle is arc length over radius.

79
00:03:17,478 --> 00:03:20,533
Length over length, so
no dimension at all.

80
00:03:20,933 --> 00:03:23,576
Frequency is how many times per second.

81
00:03:23,576 --> 00:03:25,613
That is T to the minus one.

82
00:03:26,013 --> 00:03:26,915
Your turn.

83
00:03:26,915 --> 00:03:31,138
A strain is a change in length
divided by the original length.

84
00:03:31,138 --> 00:03:33,213
Does strain have a dimension?

85
00:03:33,213 --> 00:03:34,541
Pause and decide.

86
00:03:37,741 --> 00:03:38,795
No dimension!

87
00:03:38,795 --> 00:03:41,069
Length divided by length cancels.

88
00:03:41,069 --> 00:03:44,263
Strain is a pure number,
just like an angle.

89
00:03:44,913 --> 00:03:46,648
Now, one worked example.

90
00:03:46,998 --> 00:03:49,438
Find the dimensions of momentum.

91
00:03:49,438 --> 00:03:51,877
Momentum is mass times velocity.

92
00:03:52,377 --> 00:03:53,409
Step one.

93
00:03:53,409 --> 00:03:54,579
Mass is M.

94
00:03:55,329 --> 00:03:56,242
Step two.

95
00:03:56,242 --> 00:03:58,804
Velocity is displacement over time.

96
00:03:58,804 --> 00:04:01,232
That is LT to the minus one.

97
00:04:01,982 --> 00:04:03,117
Step three.

98
00:04:03,117 --> 00:04:04,054
Multiply.

99
00:04:04,054 --> 00:04:06,741
M times LT to the minus one.

100
00:04:07,491 --> 00:04:10,315
So momentum is MLT to the minus one.

101
00:04:10,315 --> 00:04:15,142
Mass to the power one, length to the
power one, time to the power minus

102
00:04:15,142 --> 00:04:16,042
one.

103
00:04:16,315 --> 00:04:17,780
Now, the exam trap.

104
00:04:18,130 --> 00:04:22,219
Many students think a quantity with
no dimension, like an angle, needs

105
00:04:22,219 --> 00:04:23,298
no unit either.

106
00:04:23,648 --> 00:04:24,548
Not true.

107
00:04:24,464 --> 00:04:28,553
Angle is dimensionless, but it
still has a unit, the radian.

108
00:04:29,203 --> 00:04:30,531
Where is this asked?

109
00:04:30,531 --> 00:04:34,553
Short questions: the dimensions of a
quantity, or which quantities share

110
00:04:34,553 --> 00:04:35,453
them.

111
00:04:35,652 --> 00:04:36,866
Exam level now.

112
00:04:36,866 --> 00:04:40,137
Which pair of quantities
has the same dimensions?

113
00:04:40,137 --> 00:04:41,403
Pause and solve.

114
00:04:46,803 --> 00:04:48,265
The answer is C.

115
00:04:48,265 --> 00:04:50,578
Frequency and angular velocity.

116
00:04:51,078 --> 00:04:54,738
Frequency is cycles per
second, T to the minus one.

117
00:04:54,738 --> 00:04:57,311
Angular velocity is angle per second.

118
00:04:57,311 --> 00:05:01,473
Angle has no dimension, so it
is also T to the minus one.

119
00:05:01,973 --> 00:05:06,183
A is LT to the minus one
against LT to the minus two.

120
00:05:06,183 --> 00:05:08,580
B is L squared against L cubed.

121
00:05:08,580 --> 00:05:11,548
D is M against ML to the minus three.

122
00:05:12,148 --> 00:05:13,613
Here is your recap.

123
00:05:13,613 --> 00:05:15,118
Screenshot this card.

124
00:05:18,318 --> 00:05:21,154
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

125
00:05:21,554 --> 00:05:22,454
One.

126
00:05:22,072 --> 00:05:25,370
Why can you not add five
metres to five seconds?

127
00:05:26,270 --> 00:05:27,170
Two.

128
00:05:26,775 --> 00:05:29,357
What are the dimensions of acceleration?

129
00:05:30,257 --> 00:05:31,157
Three.

130
00:05:30,841 --> 00:05:32,910
Does an angle have a dimension?

131
00:05:32,910 --> 00:05:34,394
Does it have a unit?

132
00:05:35,494 --> 00:05:39,199
Next time: what is pressure
made of, in M, L and T?

133
00:05:39,199 --> 00:05:41,536
We find out in dimensional formulae.
